  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Addressing Rheumatic Heart Disease in the Pacific</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Led by the Kids Research Institute (a University of WA affiliate) this investment provides a new mechanism to grow and expand Pacific health leadership on rheumatic heart disease (RHD). Through the Fiji-based Pacific RHD Knowledge Hub it addresses the urgent unmet needs in the region. Drawing on the successful model of the Fiji RHD program UWA-TKI will work collaboratively with health authorities, community organisations and research institutions to establish and strengthen national RHD programs in Solomon Islands and Vanuatu. The program will support the establishment of country-led steering committees and participatory advisory groups to provide oversight, ownership and ensure the partnership responds to national health priorities and is integrated within the national health systems and communities. This investment is valued at $5million over four years (2024-28)</narrative>
  </description>
